# Append-only telemetry. Concurrent scan cycles (and the nightly scorecard)
# append to the same day's log, and the correct resolution is the UNION of
# both sides -- never one side winning, which silently drops observations.
# Without this, a rebase conflict on 2026-08-27T23:07Z wedged the retry loop
# and cost the tail of that day's collection.
#
# Deliberately NOT applied to docs/*.json: a union merge of JSON produces a
# broken file. Those are deterministic regenerations from logs/.
#
# CORRECTION 2026-08-31: this used to claim a lost race there "is repaired by
# the next cycle". It is NOT. A content conflict on those files wedges the
# whole RUN -- git rebase --abort restores the identical state, so every retry
# reproduces it and every later cycle inherits the same base. That cost six
# cycles and a day of peak coverage on 2026-08-30. Resolution now lives in
# .github/push_retry.sh, which takes the freshest side for exactly these
# regenerable paths and still refuses to guess on anything else.
logs/*.jsonl merge=union

# Same reasoning one level down. The H6 poller appends every 5 minutes from a
# different concurrency group than the scan, so the two WILL interleave on the
# branch; union is the correct resolution for append-only telemetry there too.
logs/poll/*.jsonl merge=union

# Windows checkout turns these into CRLF, and busybox sh dies on the :
# "syntax error: unexpected word (expecting in)" from a bare `case ... in`.
# Shipped a broken trigger image this way on 2026-08-28.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
